(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[5] = [{"v":1,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"संन्यासं कर्मणां कृष्ण पुनर्योगं च शंससि ।\nयच्छ्रेय एतयोरेकं तन्मे ब्रूहि सुनिश्चितम् ॥","iast":"saṃnyāsaṃ karmaṇāṃ kṛṣṇa punaryogaṃ ca śaṃsasi |\nyacchreya etayorekaṃ tanme brūhi suniścitam ||","read":"samnyaasam karmanaam krishna punaryogam cha shamsasi |\nyachchhreya etayorekam tanme broohi sunishchitam ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: Renunciation of actions Thou praisest, O Krishna, and then also yoga. Of the two which one is the better? That tell me conclusively.","en2":"Renunciation of action, O Krishna, thou commendest, and again, its performance. Which is the better one of these? Do thou tell me decisively.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"संन्यासः कर्मयोगश्च निःश्रेयसकरावुभौ ।\nतयोस्तु कर्मसंन्यासात्कर्मयोगो विशिष्यते ॥","iast":"saṃnyāsaḥ karmayogaśca niḥśreyasakarāvubhau |\ntayostu karmasaṃnyāsātkarmayogo viśiṣyate ||","read":"samnyaasah karmayogashcha nihshreyasakaraavubhau |\ntayostu karmasamnyaasaatkarmayogo vishishyate ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Renunciation and yoga by action both lead to the highest bliss; of the two, yoga by action is verily better than renunciation of action.","en2":"Both renunciation and performance of action lead to freedom: of these, performance of action is superior to the renunciation of action.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ज्ञेयः स नित्यसंन्यासी यो न द्वेष्टि न काङ्क्षति ।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो हि महाबाहो सुखं बन्धात्प्रमुच्यते ॥","iast":"jñeyaḥ sa nityasaṃnyāsī yo na dveṣṭi na kāṅkṣati |\nnirdvandvo hi mahābāho sukhaṃ bandhātpramucyate ||","read":"jneyah sa nityasamnyaasee yo na dveshti na kaankshati |\nnirdvandvo hi mahaabaaho sukham bandhaatpramuchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He should be known as a perpetual ascetic, who neither hateth nor desireth; free from the pairs of opposites, O mighty-armed, he is easily set free from bondage.","en2":"He should be known a constant Sannyâsi, who neither likes nor dislikes: for, free from the pairs of opposites, mighty-armed, he is easily set free from bondage.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सांख्ययोगौ पृथग्बालाः प्रवदन्ति न पण्डिताः ।\nएकमप्यास्थितः सम्यगुभयोर्विन्दते फलम् ॥","iast":"sāṃkhyayogau pṛthagbālāḥ pravadanti na paṇḍitāḥ |\nekamapyāsthitaḥ samyagubhayorvindate phalam ||","read":"saamkhyayogau prithagbaalaah pravadanti na panditaah |\nekamapyaasthitah samyagubhayorvindate phalam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Children, not sages, speak of the Sânkhya and the Yoga as different; he who is duly established in one obtaineth the fruits of both.","en2":"Children, not the wise, speak of knowledge and performance of action, as distinct. He who truly lives in one, gains the fruits of both.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यत्सांख्यैः प्राप्यते स्थानं तद्योगैरपि गम्यते ।\nएकं सांख्यं च योगं च यः पश्यति स पश्यति ॥","iast":"yatsāṃkhyaiḥ prāpyate sthānaṃ tadyogairapi gamyate |\nekaṃ sāṃkhyaṃ ca yogaṃ ca yaḥ paśyati sa paśyati ||","read":"yatsaamkhyaih praapyate sthaanam tadyogairapi gamyate |\nekam saamkhyam cha yogam cha yah pashyati sa pashyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That place which is gained by the Sânkhyas is reached by the Yogîs also. He seeth, who seeth that the Sânkhya and the Yoga are one.","en2":"The plane which is reached by the Jnânins is also reached by the Karmayogins. Who sees knowledge and performance of action as one, he sees.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"संन्यासस्तु महाबाहो दुःखमाप्तुमयोगतः ।\nयोगयुक्तो मुनिर्ब्रह्म नचिरेणाधिगच्छति ॥","iast":"saṃnyāsastu mahābāho duḥkhamāptumayogataḥ |\nyogayukto munirbrahma nacireṇādhigacchati ||","read":"samnyaasastu mahaabaaho duhkhamaaptumayogatah |\nyogayukto munirbrahma nachirenaadhigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But without yoga, O mighty-armed, renunciation is hard to attain to; the yoga-harmonised Muni swiftly goeth to the Eternal.","en2":"Renunciation of action, O mighty-armed, is hard to attain to without performance of action; the man of meditation, purified by devotion to action, quickly goes to Brahman.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"योगयुक्तो विशुद्धात्मा विजितात्मा जितेन्द्रियः ।\nसर्वभूतात्मभूतात्मा कुर्वन्नपि न लिप्यते ॥","iast":"yogayukto viśuddhātmā vijitātmā jitendriyaḥ |\nsarvabhūtātmabhūtātmā kurvannapi na lipyate ||","read":"yogayukto vishuddhaatmaa vijitaatmaa jitendriyah |\nsarvabhootaatmabhootaatmaa kurvannapi na lipyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who is harmonised by yoga, the self purified, Self -ruled, the senses subdued, whose Self is the Self of all beings, although acting he is not affected.","en2":"With the mind purified by devotion to performance of action, and the body conquered, and senses subdued, one who realises one's Self, as the Self in all beings, though acting, is not tainted.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नैव किञ्चित्करोमीति युक्तो मन्येत तत्त्ववित् ।\nपश्यञ्शृण्वन्स्पृशञ्जिघ्रन्नश्नन्गच्छन्स्वपञ्श्वसन् ॥","iast":"naiva kiñcitkaromīti yukto manyeta tattvavit |\npaśyañśṛṇvanspṛśañjighrannaśnangacchansvapañśvasan ||","read":"naiva kinchitkaromeeti yukto manyeta tattvavit |\npashyanshrinvansprishanjighrannashnangachchhansvapanshvasan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"\"I do not anything,\" should think the harmonised one, who knoweth the essence of things; seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, moving, sleeping, breathing.","en2":"The knower of Truth, (being) centred (in the Self) should think, \"I do nothing at all\"—though seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, going, sleeping, breathing, speaking, letting go, holding, opening and closing the eyes—convinced that it is the senses that move among sense-objects.","en2r":"5.8-9","rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रलपन्विसृजन्गृह्णन्नुन्मिषन्निमिषन्नपि ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेषु वर्तन्त इति धारयन् ॥","iast":"pralapanvisṛjangṛhṇannunmiṣannimiṣannapi |\nindriyāṇīndriyārtheṣu vartanta iti dhārayan ||","read":"pralapanvisrijangrihnannunmishannimishannapi |\nindriyaaneendriyaartheshu vartanta iti dhaarayan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Speaking, giving, grasping, opening and closing the eyes, he holdeth: \"The senses move among the objects of the senses.\"","en2":"The knower of Truth, (being) centred (in the Self) should think, \"I do nothing at all\"—though seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, going, sleeping, breathing, speaking, letting go, holding, opening and closing the eyes—convinced that it is the senses that move among sense-objects.","en2r":"5.8-9","rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ब्रह्मण्याधाय कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा करोति यः ।\nलिप्यते न स पापेन पद्मपत्रमिवाम्भसा ॥","iast":"brahmaṇyādhāya karmāṇi saṅgaṃ tyaktvā karoti yaḥ |\nlipyate na sa pāpena padmapatramivāmbhasā ||","read":"brahmanyaadhaaya karmaani sangam tyaktvaa karoti yah |\nlipyate na sa paapena padmapatramivaambhasaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who acteth, placing all actions in the Eternal, abandoning attachment, is unaffected by sin as a lotus leaf by the waters.","en2":"He who does actions forsaking attachment, resigning them to Brahman, is not soiled by evil, like unto a lotus-leaf by water.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कायेन मनसा बुद्ध्या केवलैरिन्द्रियैरपि ।\nयोगिनः कर्म कुर्वन्ति सङ्गं त्यक्त्वाऽऽत्मशुद्धये ॥","iast":"kāyena manasā buddhyā kevalairindriyairapi |\nyoginaḥ karma kurvanti saṅgaṃ tyaktvā’’tmaśuddhaye ||","read":"kaayena manasaa buddhyaa kevalairindriyairapi |\nyoginah karma kurvanti sangam tyaktvaa''tmashuddhaye ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Yogis, having abandoned attachment, perform action only by the body, by the mind, by the Reason, and even by the senses, for the purification of the self.","en2":"Devotees in the path of work perform action, only with body, mind, senses, and intellect, forsaking attachment, for the purification of the heart.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"युक्तः कर्मफलं त्यक्त्वा शान्तिमाप्नोति नैष्ठिकीम् ।\nअयुक्तः कामकारेण फले सक्तो निबध्यते ॥","iast":"yuktaḥ karmaphalaṃ tyaktvā śāntimāpnoti naiṣṭhikīm |\nayuktaḥ kāmakāreṇa phale sakto nibadhyate ||","read":"yuktah karmaphalam tyaktvaa shaantimaapnoti naishthikeem |\nayuktah kaamakaarena phale sakto nibadhyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The harmonised man, having abandoned the fruit of action, attaineth to the eternal Peace; the non-harmonised, impelled by desire, attached to fruit, are bound.","en2":"The well-poised, forsaking the fruit of action, attains peace, born of steadfastness; the unbalanced one, led by desire, is bound by being attached to the fruit (of action).","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वकर्माणि मनसा संन्यस्यास्ते सुखं वशी ।\nनवद्वारे पुरे देही नैव कुर्वन्न कारयन् ॥","iast":"sarvakarmāṇi manasā saṃnyasyāste sukhaṃ vaśī |\nnavadvāre pure dehī naiva kurvanna kārayan ||","read":"sarvakarmaani manasaa samnyasyaaste sukham vashee |\nnavadvaare pure dehee naiva kurvanna kaarayan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Mentally renouncing all actions, the sovereign dweller in the body resteth serenely in the nine-gated city, neither acting nor causing to act.","en2":"The subduer (of the senses), having renounced all actions by discrimination, rests happily in the city of the nine gates, neither acting, nor causing (others) to act.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न कर्तृत्वं न कर्माणि लोकस्य सृजति प्रभुः ।\nन कर्मफलसंयोगं स्वभावस्तु प्रवर्तते ॥","iast":"na kartṛtvaṃ na karmāṇi lokasya sṛjati prabhuḥ |\nna karmaphalasaṃyogaṃ svabhāvastu pravartate ||","read":"na kartritvam na karmaani lokasya srijati prabhuh |\nna karmaphalasamyogam svabhaavastu pravartate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Lord of the world produceth not the idea of agency, nor actions, nor the union together of action and its fruit; nature, however, manifesteth.","en2":"Neither agency, nor actions does the Lord create for the world, nor (does He bring about) the union with the fruit of action. It is universal ignorance that does. (it all).","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नादत्ते कस्यचित्पापं न चैव सुकृतं विभुः ।\nअज्ञानेनावृतं ज्ञानं तेन मुह्यन्ति जन्तवः ॥","iast":"nādatte kasyacitpāpaṃ na caiva sukṛtaṃ vibhuḥ |\najñānenāvṛtaṃ jñānaṃ tena muhyanti jantavaḥ ||","read":"naadatte kasyachitpaapam na chaiva sukritam vibhuh |\najnaanenaavritam jnaanam tena muhyanti jantavah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Lord accepteth neither the evil-doing nor yet the well-doing of any. Wisdom is enveloped by unwisdom; therewith mortals are deluded.","en2":"The Omnipresent takes note of the merit or demerit of none. Knowledge is enveloped in ignorance, hence do beings get deluded.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ज्ञानेन तु तदज्ञानं येषां नाशितमात्मनः ।\nतेषामादित्यवज्ज्ञानं प्रकाशयति तत्परम् ॥","iast":"jñānena tu tadajñānaṃ yeṣāṃ nāśitamātmanaḥ |\nteṣāmādityavajjñānaṃ prakāśayati tatparam ||","read":"jnaanena tu tadajnaanam yeshaam naashitamaatmanah |\nteshaamaadityavajjnaanam prakaashayati tatparam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Verily, in whom unwisdom is destroyed by the wisdom of the Self, in them wisdom, shining as the sun, reveals the Supreme.","en2":"But whose ignorance is destroyed by the knowledge of Self,—that knowledge of theirs, like the sun, reveals the Supreme (Brahman).","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तद्बुद्धयस्तदात्मानस्तन्निष्ठास्तत्परायणाः ।\nगच्छन्त्यपुनरावृत्तिं ज्ञाननिर्धूतकल्मषाः ॥","iast":"tadbuddhayastadātmānastanniṣṭhāstatparāyaṇāḥ |\ngacchantyapunarāvṛttiṃ jñānanirdhūtakalmaṣāḥ ||","read":"tadbuddhayastadaatmaanastannishthaastatparaayanaah |\ngachchhantyapunaraavrittim jnaananirdhootakalmashaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Thinking on That, merged in That, established in That, solely devoted to That, they go whence there is no return, their sins dispelled by wisdom.","en2":"Those who have their intellect absorbed in That, whose self is That, whose steadfastness is in That, whose consummation is That, their impurities cleansed by knowledge, they attain to Non-return (Moksha).","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"विद्याविनयसंपन्ने ब्राह्मणे गवि हस्तिनि ।\nशुनि चैव श्वपाके च पण्डिताः समदर्शिनः ॥","iast":"vidyāvinayasaṃpanne brāhmaṇe gavi hastini |\nśuni caiva śvapāke ca paṇḍitāḥ samadarśinaḥ ||","read":"vidyaavinayasampanne braahmane gavi hastini |\nshuni chaiva shvapaake cha panditaah samadarshinah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Sages look equally on a Brâhmana adorned with learning and humility, a cow, an elephant, and even a dog and an outcaste.","en2":"The knowers of the Self look with an equal eye on a Brâhmana endowed with learning and humility, a cow, an elephant, a dog, and a pariah.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इहैव तैर्जितः सर्गो येषां साम्ये स्थितं मनः ।\nनिर्दोषं हि समं ब्रह्म तस्माद्ब्रह्मणि ते स्थिताः ॥","iast":"ihaiva tairjitaḥ sargo yeṣāṃ sāmye sthitaṃ manaḥ |\nnirdoṣaṃ hi samaṃ brahma tasmādbrahmaṇi te sthitāḥ ||","read":"ihaiva tairjitah sargo yeshaam saamye sthitam manah |\nnirdosham hi samam brahma tasmaadbrahmani te sthitaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Even here on earth everything is overcome by those whose mind remains balanced; the Eternal is incorruptible and balanced; therefore they are established in the Eternal.","en2":"(Relative) existence has been conquered by them, even in this world, whose mind rests in evenness, since Brahman is even and without imperfection: therefore they indeed rest in Brahman.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न प्रहृष्येत्प्रियं प्राप्य नोद्विजेत्प्राप्य चाप्रियम् ।\nस्थिरबुद्धिरसम्मूढो ब्रह्मविद्ब्रह्मणि स्थितः ॥","iast":"na prahṛṣyetpriyaṃ prāpya nodvijetprāpya cāpriyam |\nsthirabuddhirasammūḍho brahmavidbrahmaṇi sthitaḥ ||","read":"na prahrishyetpriyam praapya nodvijetpraapya chaapriyam |\nsthirabuddhirasammoodho brahmavidbrahmani sthitah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"With Reason firm, unperplexed, the knower of the Eternal established in the Eternal, neither rejoiceth on obtaining what is pleasant, nor sorroweth on obtaining what is unpleasant.","en2":"Resting in Brahman, with intellect steady, and without delusion, the knower of Brahman neither rejoiceth on receiving what is pleasant, nor grieveth on receiving what is unpleasant.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बाह्यस्पर्शेष्वसक्तात्मा विन्दत्यात्मनि यत्सुखम् ।\nस ब्रह्मयोगयुक्तात्मा सुखमक्षयमश्नुते ॥","iast":"bāhyasparśeṣvasaktātmā vindatyātmani yatsukham |\nsa brahmayogayuktātmā sukhamakṣayamaśnute ||","read":"baahyasparsheshvasaktaatmaa vindatyaatmani yatsukham |\nsa brahmayogayuktaatmaa sukhamakshayamashnute ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He, whose self is unattached to external contacts and findeth joy in the Self, having the self harmonised with the Eternal by yoga, enjoys imperishable bliss.","en2":"With the heart unattached to external objects, he realises the joy that is in the Self. With the heart devoted to the meditation of Brahman, he attains un-decaying happiness.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ये हि संस्पर्शजा भोगा दुःखयोनय एव ते ।\nआद्यन्तवन्तः कौन्तेय न तेषु रमते बुधः ॥","iast":"ye hi saṃsparśajā bhogā duḥkhayonaya eva te |\nādyantavantaḥ kaunteya na teṣu ramate budhaḥ ||","read":"ye hi samsparshajaa bhogaa duhkhayonaya eva te |\naadyantavantah kaunteya na teshu ramate budhah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The delights that are contact-born, they are verily wombs of pain, for they have beginning and ending, O Kaunteya; not in them may rejoice the wise.","en2":"Since enjoyments that are contact-born are parents of misery alone, and with beginning and end, O son of Kunti, a wise man does not seek pleasure in them.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"शक्नोतीहैव यः सोढुं प्राक्शरीरविमोक्षणात् ।\nकामक्रोधोद्भवं वेगं स युक्तः स सुखी नरः ॥","iast":"śaknotīhaiva yaḥ soḍhuṃ prākśarīravimokṣaṇāt |\nkāmakrodhodbhavaṃ vegaṃ sa yuktaḥ sa sukhī naraḥ ||","read":"shaknoteehaiva yah sodhum praakshareeravimokshanaat |\nkaamakrodhodbhavam vegam sa yuktah sa sukhee narah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who is able to endure here on earth, ere he be liberated from the body, the force born from desire and passion, he is harmonised, he is a happy man.","en2":"He who can withstand in this world, before the liberation from the body, the impulse arising from lust and anger, he is steadfast (in Yoga), he is a happy man.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"योऽन्तःसुखोऽन्तरारामस्तथान्तर्ज्योतिरेव यः ।\nस योगी ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं ब्रह्मभूतोऽधिगच्छति ॥","iast":"yo’ntaḥsukho’ntarārāmastathāntarjyotireva yaḥ |\nsa yogī brahmanirvāṇaṃ brahmabhūto’dhigacchati ||","read":"yo'ntahsukho'ntaraaraamastathaantarjyotireva yah |\nsa yogee brahmanirvaanam brahmabhooto'dhigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who is happy within, who rejoiceth within, who is illuminated within, that Yogî, becoming the Eternal, goeth to the Peace of the Eternal.","en2":"Whose happiness is within, whose relaxation is within, whose light is within, that Yogi alone, becoming Brahman, gains absolute freedom.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"लभन्ते ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृषयः क्षीणकल्मषाः ।\nछिन्नद्वैधा यतात्मानः सर्वभूतहिते रताः ॥","iast":"labhante brahmanirvāṇamṛṣayaḥ kṣīṇakalmaṣāḥ |\nchinnadvaidhā yatātmānaḥ sarvabhūtahite ratāḥ ||","read":"labhante brahmanirvaanamrishayah ksheenakalmashaah |\nchhinnadvaidhaa yataatmaanah sarvabhootahite rataah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Rishis, their sins destroyed, their duality removed, their selves controlled, intent upon the welfare of all beings, obtain the Peace of the Eternal.","en2":"With imperfections exhausted, doubts dispelled, senses controlled, engaged in the good of all beings, the Rishis obtain absolute freedom.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कामक्रोधवियुक्तानां यतीनां यतचेतसाम् ।\nअभितो ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं वर्तते विदितात्मनाम् ॥","iast":"kāmakrodhaviyuktānāṃ yatīnāṃ yatacetasām |\nabhito brahmanirvāṇaṃ vartate viditātmanām ||","read":"kaamakrodhaviyuktaanaam yateenaam yatachetasaam |\nabhito brahmanirvaanam vartate viditaatmanaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Peace of the Eternal lies near to those who know themselves, who are disjoined from desire and passion, subdued in nature, of subdued thoughts.","en2":"Released from lust and anger, the heart controlled, the Self realised, absolute freedom is for such Sannyâsis, both here and hereafter.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"स्पर्शान्कृत्वा बहिर्बाह्यांश्चक्षुश्चैवान्तरे भ्रुवोः ।\nप्राणापानौ समौ कृत्वा नासाभ्यन्तरचारिणौ ॥","iast":"sparśānkṛtvā bahirbāhyāṃścakṣuścaivāntare bhruvoḥ |\nprāṇāpānau samau kṛtvā nāsābhyantaracāriṇau ||","read":"sparshaankritvaa bahirbaahyaamshchakshushchaivaantare bhruvoh |\npraanaapaanau samau kritvaa naasaabhyantarachaarinau ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having external contacts excluded, and with gaze fixed between the eyebrows; having made equal the outgoing and ingoing breaths moving within the nostrils;","en2":"Shutting out external objects, steadying the eyes between the eyebrows, restricting the even currents of Prâna and Apâna inside the nostrils; the senses, mind, and intellect controlled, with Moksha as the supreme goal, freed from desire, fear and anger: such a man of meditation is verily free for ever.","en2r":"5.27-28","rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यतेन्द्रियमनोबुद्धिर्मुनिर्मोक्षपरायणः ।\nविगतेच्छाभयक्रोधो यः सदा मुक्त एव सः ॥","iast":"yatendriyamanobuddhirmunirmokṣaparāyaṇaḥ |\nvigatecchābhayakrodho yaḥ sadā mukta eva saḥ ||","read":"yatendriyamanobuddhirmunirmokshaparaayanah |\nvigatechchhaabhayakrodho yah sadaa mukta eva sah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"With senses, mind, and Reason ever controlled, solely pursuing liberation, the Sage, having for ever cast away desire, fear and passion, verily is liberated.","en2":"Shutting out external objects, steadying the eyes between the eyebrows, restricting the even currents of Prâna and Apâna inside the nostrils; the senses, mind, and intellect controlled, with Moksha as the supreme goal, freed from desire, fear and anger: such a man of meditation is verily free for ever.","en2r":"5.27-28","rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"भोक्तारं यज्ञतपसां सर्वलोकमहेश्वरम् ।\nसुहृदं सर्वभूतानां ज्ञात्वा मां शान्तिमृच्छति ॥","iast":"bhoktāraṃ yajñatapasāṃ sarvalokamaheśvaram |\nsuhṛdaṃ sarvabhūtānāṃ jñātvā māṃ śāntimṛcchati ||","read":"bhoktaaram yajnatapasaam sarvalokamaheshvaram |\nsuhridam sarvabhootaanaam jnaatvaa maam shaantimrichchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having known Me, as the Enjoyer of sacrifice and of austerity, the mighty Ruler of all the worlds, and the Lover of all beings, he goeth to Peace.","en2":"Knowing Me as the dispenser of Yajnas and asceticisms, as the Great Lord of all worlds, as the friend of all beings, he attains Peace.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null}];
